    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-8952-3",
        "name": "USN-8952-3",
        "description": "USN-8952-2 fixed a regression in Tornado that broke static file serving for applications that subclass Tornado's StaticFileHandler, such as Jupyter. Unfortunately, that update's incomplete fix could introduce a regression by rejecting symlinks into system directories like /usr/share, which distribution packages use for their JavaScript and fonts, causing web UIs to return 403 errors. This update fixes the problem.  We apologize for the inconvenience.  Original advisory details:   It was discovered that Tornado did not properly handle certain HTTP requests  and network inputs. An attacker could possibly use these issues to cause a  denial of service, expose sensitive information, or bypass access controls.   (CVE-2023-54397, CVE-2024-14029, CVE-2026-91990, CVE-2026-91992,  CVE-2026-103262, CVE-2026-103263)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2026-103263"
        ]
      },
      "timestamp": "2026-11-11T08:15:26Z",
